layed H4, a point White took later at move 32. The move made the center wall bigger, but it left the right-side gap open."}, {"turn": 29, "text": "B1 was Opus 5.5's worst move, losing 7.1 points and sinking Black from -5.4 to -12.5. White had just played A1 and captured a stone, and the engine's choice was F7. After B1, White's C1 pushed the lead out to -12.7 and the game was effectively settled."}, {"turn": 28, "text": "The 14k's biggest slip was A1, which lost 4.5 points, though Black's lead only moved from -9.9 to -5.4 and Opus 5.5 was still well behind. White captured a stone with it. Opus 5.5 did not use the opening, since the next move lost 7.1 points."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberties, flagging groups with two or fewer. count.py flood-fills regions to count territory for a position, with named stones treated as dead. Both only inspect the current position, and neither chooses, ranks or looks ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}